WEBVTT

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.450
"WINNER MATENRO"

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.500
All right! We did it!

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.410
Yes! We did it! We won!

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:30.790
Doppo, Hifumi, we did a fine job.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.290
"Matenro Wins!"

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.660
"First Division Rap Battle Tournament
Matenro Wins!"

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.830
The victor is Shinjuku's Matenro.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.540
Such excitement.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:59.330
It appears the division rap battle has
had more of an impact than we had imagined.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:03.750
Yes, it has. We expect the four teams
that fought in the final tournament

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.120
will be considered national
heroes from this day forth.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.540
If that happens,
their usefulness would be limitless.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.410
Seeing that the Ramuda Amemura
project has failed,

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:17.000
I believe we should
devise a new plan immediately.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.950
A new plan?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:23.790
We shall capture the four teams swiftly
and perform a mind hack on them.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.790
If we make them puppets of the Party of Words,

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:30.950
the general public will also
be at the party's command.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.290
Very well. I will allow it.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:37.160
Your ideals are our ideals, Ms. Otome.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.870
I assure you I shall succeed.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.000
"Matenro"

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.200
We did it! We are the champions!

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.120
Ever since I was born, there was never
a time I felt I'd accomplished something.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.200
Yep, yep, you said it.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.040
Me--the dilly-dallying, dimwitted water flea...

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.330
Yep, yep, you said it.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:32.330
Me--who has been called a salary thief
by my balding boss at work...

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.370
Yep, yep, you said it.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:35.700
Um...

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.540
Isn't there something that you can deny?

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:41.250
Huh? Why? Isn't it the truth?

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.200
There must be something!

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.790
Sure there is. Now let's look
for it together, Doppomine!

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.370
Ouch!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:54.540
Hifumi, Doppo, thanks to the two of you
we were able to win the championship.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:04:00.040
The two of you trusted
your abilities and gave it your all.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.040
Allow me to thank you once again.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.450
There's no need to thank us.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.870
We're a team, aren't we?

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.160
You're right.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.120
Then, let us commend
each other for our hard work!

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.830
Doctor!

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:18.040
I hope I'm not disturbing you.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:21.500
--Eek!
--I'm with the Party of Words.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.330
I'm here to take you to see the Prime Minister.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.620
The Prime Minister?

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.450
We get to meet the Prime Minister?

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:29.790
Seriously?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:37.620
A hypnosis mic had been used to place
Yotsutsuji under a powerful hypnosis.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:40.330
The ones capable of
making such a device would be...

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.200
All right.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.200
There is something
I would like to ask the Prime Minister.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.870
Then, come this way.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:53.410
I realize you're pissed off,
but that's damage you're 100 percent liable for.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:55.450
Like I give a fuck!

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.370
Rio. Why don't you try calming him down?

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.870
At the rate he's going, before we leave

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.830
I'm going to have to arrest him
for criminal destruction of property.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.830
If that happens, you'd take the credit for it.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.500
I'm sorry, but I'm occupied at the moment.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.250
What are you doing?

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.790
I'm applying a mixture of magnesium
and an ignition agent around a smoke bomb.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.790
What?

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.450
Don't you see? It's a flash bomb.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:22.330
How would I know that?!

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.450
First of all, what do you
plan on doing with that?

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.120
This is the chance of a lifetime.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.500
Men are hardly ever allowed inside Chuohku.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.830
The lieutenant commander is
incarcerated somewhere inside this place.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.160
Rio, you aren't going to--

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:43.450
The high I felt fighting alongside you
in battle has strengthened my resolve.

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.910
I shall rescue the lieutenant commander.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:48.080
You're bound to fail, you know?

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.660
Stop him, Samatoki!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.620
Rio's right.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.790
We don't know the next time
we'll be able to come here.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.540
That means now's
my only chance to look for Nemu.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.080
Now just a minute there!

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.620
I hope I'm not disturbing you.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.330
What do you want?

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:06.620
I'm here to take you to see the Prime Minister.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:07.950
The Prime Minister?

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.410
Oh, I get it.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.910
If we meet that dame, I might
be able to find out what I wanna know.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:13.450
About your younger sister?

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:16.830
Yeah. I got lots of stuff I wanna ask that dame.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.250
Wait!

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.620
We get to meet the Prime Minister?

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.790
That's awesome, Big Bro!

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.750
Brother Ichi!

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.870
Could you come over here for a second?

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:30.250
What's up?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:36.370
Ever since we got here,
I've been trying to hack into Chuohku's system.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.540
What'd you do something like that for?!

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.120
Keep it down, you idiot!

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.660
Take a look at this.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.040
These are the surveillance cameras
in this building.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.450
This room is surrounded.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:49.250
Are these gals Special Forces?

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.000
Why would they be--?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.790
I don't know.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:54.290
But what I do know is that

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:57.000
it doesn't look like they're going
to let us go home peacefully.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
What should we do, Big Bro?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.870
At a time like this, it's quicker and
easier to just ask them point-blank.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.290
What's this all about?

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.790
What's wrong, Doctor?

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:17.040
I'm a man who has been
through hell several times now.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.910
It's made me aware of
when danger is close at hand.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.700
What danger are you talking about?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.910
I do not know the details.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:28.200
But I smell something suspicious.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:31.120
It may be best if we made a break for it.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:33.200
We won't let you do that!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.330
What's this?

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.040
Thermography.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.160
This room is surrounded.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.790
What's the big idea here?

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.660
You got some explainin' to do!

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:50.330
You should just follow orders.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:54.000
I would advise against using
that word in front of Mr. Samatoki here.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.000
Orders, huh?

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.950
There ain't a soul on this planet
that can order me around, bitch!

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:03.750
Then we'll take you there by force!

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.450
We ain't scared of ya! We'll take ya all on!

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:13.290
The three members of Fling Posse aren't here.
We believe they've already escaped.

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:16.750
Ramuda Amemura has the true hypnosis mic.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:20.160
Do not, I repeat, do not let him get away!

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:24.080
It doesn't matter how many of you come at us.
We are unstoppable!

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.410
Samatoki!

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:28.790
Ichiro! You're still hangin' around here?!

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:31.620
I'll fight you again,
and this time I won't lose!

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:34.540
Huh? In your dreams, asshole!

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:39.580
Samatoki! Ichiro Yamada!
Now's not the time to be at each other's throats!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.750
Other units are on their way here!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.250
We're calling a truce for now!

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.200
All right! Quit your whinin'!

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:50.450
Buster Bros!!! MAD TRIGGER CREW! This way!

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:53.200
--You're--!
--You were with Tom.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.580
We'll lead the way. Follow us.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.290
After them!

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.580
Say "Cheese!"

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.040
Now! Before it's too late!

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:08.370
You've been a great help!

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.450
What's the matter, Dice?

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.330
I'm tired from running.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:20.790
Why do we gotta leave in such a rush?

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.500
I concur with him.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:25.540
Huh? Look! After an event is over,

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:29.620
everyone leaves all at once, so the trains
and buses get super crowded, right?

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:30.910
You've got a point there.

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:33.160
But we made it to the finals.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.910
There's gotta be a taxi waitin'
to take us home, right?

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:36.450
What are you talking about?

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.000
The losing teams don't get any perks like that!

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.290
Chuohku is currently
experiencing financial difficulties!

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.160
Everyone's gotta take the train or walk!

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.120
Considering they can
shell out 100 mil in prize money,

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.540
that's surprisingly stingy of them.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.790
That's right! Chuohku's stingy!

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:50.700
Now that you know, let's get moving!

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:53.450
Hold, Ramuda, prithee wait a little.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.790
Was there something else?

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.620
It seemeth that thou art unaware of this, but

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:01.370
when thou liest, thy right eyebrow twitcheth.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.080
Huh? I have a habit like that?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.000
--Nay.
--Huh?

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.500
What I said just now was but a lie.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:12.410
Yet now we know that thou hadst been lying.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:16.330
For thee, who art ever so cautious,
to be deceived so completely,

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:18.540
thou must be in quite a hurry.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:22.410
Tell us the truth. What are you hidin', Ramuda?

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:31.450
All right, already! I'll level with you!

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:35.290
If we get caught by the Chuohku gals,
they'll do something terrible to us.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:38.750
They're trying to brainwash and use us.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:41.580
Brainwash us? Why would they do that?

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:44.120
All of us finalists are big stars.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.950
The Party of Words is going
to take advantage of that.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:50.290
Ah, so that is what the Party of Words is--

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:53.330
But why do <i>you </i>know about it?

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.410
W-Well...

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:58.160
I overheard them saying that!

00:10:58.160 --> 00:10:59.870
Hmm...

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:03.500
My right eyebrow's not twitching, is it?

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:07.160
I see. But that don't mean
it's okay for us to just take off

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.080
and leave the other teams behind.

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:12.700
I concur with him. 'Twould grieveth me so.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:15.700
We don't have time to be
worrying about the other teams!

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:18.500
Those gals are a real dangerous bunch!

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:20.330
If they catch us...

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:23.120
...they'll kill me for sure!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.620
Then we most certainly
cannot leave things as they stand.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.370
Argh!

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:31.040
Well then, why don't we use
<i>these </i>to decide what to do?

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.000
Dr. Jakurai!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.410
The Chuohku broads are after you guys, too?

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:41.370
Ichiro. Samatoki. Not you as well?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:45.660
Yeah, us too.
The Party of Words tried to capture us.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.080
And these guys saved us.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.910
Tom. You were here, too?

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:54.330
Yeah. I got permission to cover a story.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.160
Come. We'll show you the way.

00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:00.080
What the hell could they be up to?

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:02.330
You'll find out soon enough.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:17.290
What the--?!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.120
You're here at last.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:23.370
Matenro!

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:24.830
Buster Bros!!!

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:27.040
MAD TRIGGER CREW!

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.250
You've caused us a great deal of trouble.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:37.200
You're the special advisor
to the prime minister...

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:40.080
...Ichijiku Kadenokoji, was it?

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.870
Good work!

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:45.450
I'm sorry, Ichiro, Dr. Jakurai.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.790
What's this all about, Tom?

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.450
It's simple really.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:57.330
They've been on our side from the beginning.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:58.620
What did you say?

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.540
They are Secret Aliens.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.830
Secret Aliens?

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:06.330
I have heard the rumors.

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:10.830
That in times of national crisis,
there is a group of soldiers who work

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:15.080
behind the scenes to assist freedom-loving
governments and revolutionaries.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:18.200
So, you guys are that group, Tom?

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:21.750
That's right. We are Secret Aliens.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.660
National crisis?

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:29.000
That makes it sound like we're
a bunch of thugs that threaten the peace.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:34.950
Surely you all must realize
that we are not a threat to freedom.

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:42.200
Yes, we do. Matenro, Buster Bros!!!,
MAD TRIGGER CREW, and Fling Posse.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.000
After watching your battles,

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:49.950
we could see that your spirits are
full of freedom, hope, and courage.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:51.500
Then why?!

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:54.580
You can't make an omelet without breaking eggs.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.500
What'd he say just now?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:59.700
"You can't make an omelet
without breaking eggs."

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:03.870
What he means is that sacrifices must be
made in order to achieve something great.

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:07.200
An omelet? So, we're the eggs?

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.410
And we've got to get broken?

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:12.500
Your power is too wild.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:18.870
Someday its influence could grow so large
that it could oppose the Party of Words.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.160
And that scares me.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.580
Why are you afraid of somethin' like that?

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:28.250
Through the power of hypnosis mics,
the Party of Words's revolution

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:34.290
rid this country of weapons and
saved many people from senseless violence.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.620
If the Party of Words were to cease to exist,

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:40.120
public order would return to how it was
when the country relied on weapons,

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.950
and it would resume fighting with other nations.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:47.120
So, I concluded that we should
protect the Party of Words for now.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:52.160
For a huge creature to survive,
some critters have got to be sacrificed.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.290
And you're saying that's us?

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.500
Don't give us that crap!

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:59.250
Ain't no way we're gonna be sacrificed
for your selfish, bullshit theories!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.580
We'll kick all your asses right here, right now!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.120
You'll be fighting <i>us</i>, you know?!

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:07.450
There are nine of us.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:09.870
Are you saying you're going
to take us all on at once?

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:11.200
Don't worry.

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:14.040
We can scatter that many foes with ease.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.370
Don't you go takin' us
for a bunch of fools! Here we go!

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.790
C'mon now, hurry up and put this on!

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.410
It's my turn, huh?

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.660
Here we go!

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:32.250
Ichiro! Samatoki! Doctor!
I've been wanting a chance to fight you!

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:45.450
♬ Let me kick open the door to reality ♬

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:49.580
♬ I'm getting a glimpse of the world beyond ♬

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:53.580
♬ Seen it before is my impression ♬

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:59.370
--♬ Two, three, four, five, six... seventh dimension ♬
--♬ Yeah uh, Bring it in ♬

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.660
♬ Look up in the sky ♬

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:10.080
♬ You can't do anything if you just fight ♬

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:13.160
♬ Yeah, Secret Aliens ♬

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.330
♬ My pack will track you down wherever you go ♬

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.870
♬ You know?
One word rounds 'em up like so ♬

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.000
♬ If it's survival of the
fittest then I'm the biggest ♬

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.620
--♬ Obviously ♬
--♬ Capitalism on my mind ♬

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:25.500
--♬ Basically we up high ♬
--♬ And that's nothing to hypothesize ♬

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.200
♪ Like a T-rex
I'll bite those who stand in my way ♪

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.700
--♬ Immediate takeover ♬
--♬ Haters
The last card pulled-- JOKER ♬

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.500
--♬ Slow down... Move over ♬
--♬ Haters
The last card pulled-- JOKER ♬

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.540
♬ Follow me, a chance in this world to succeed ♬

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:36.620
♬ I'm feelin it, the losers gonna concede ♬

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.620
♬ If you didn't know before, I guess you know now! ♬

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.830
♬ This system where winning shouldn't be possible ♬

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:42.830
♬ Let's march into Babylon ♬

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.830
♬ Y'all already know who we are ♬

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:49.370
--♬ Secret Aliens
Come on! ♬
--♬ Let me kick open the door to reality ♬

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:53.370
♬ I'm getting a glimpse of the world beyond ♬

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:57.370
♬ Seen it before is my impression ♬

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:03.450
♬ Two, three, four, five, six... seventh dimension ♬

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:17.160
--What the hell was that?
--Their attack is in a league of its own.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:18.830
Well done.

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:21.660
Just what you'd expect from foes
who said they'd take us all on at once.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.580
Such formidable opponents...

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:26.120
C'mon, it's your turn to attack!

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:31.620
With this much damage,
I will have to heal everyone first.

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:35.410
The speakers have vanished?!

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:37.250
That ain't all!

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.330
Our mics--!

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:42.250
What the hell's going on here?!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:45.910
So, it seems they have perfected it.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.910
The hypnosis canceller I have here

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:51.950
will completely disable the effects
of specific mics within its range.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:54.120
So, you went and made a thing like that, huh?

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.950
When you make a vehicle with a powerful engine,

00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:00.660
you must also make
some powerful brakes to stop it.

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:03.160
It's only natural.

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:06.580
Now there is no longer
any way for you to resist us!

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.540
Capture them!

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.950
Not like this!

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:11.950
You bitch!

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:13.250
What the--?!

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:15.540
Oh, I went and did it.

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:17.250
You ain't got nothin' to complain about.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:19.370
I beat you fair and square.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:22.330
Damn, that's the first time
I ever cheated in my whole life.

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:27.370
And while we are at it,
let us pull out all the stops.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.910
What is it this time?!

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:30.870
Everybody, close your eyes!

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.750
What is the meaning of this?

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.700
We agreed to assist you in exchange for

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:46.120
the chance to fight Ichiro
and the others in a fair match.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:48.870
You didn't say anything
about using a hypnosis canceller.

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:56.950
I hear that you have ties with
a refugee camp in the Republic of Moralia.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:19:00.370
There are many children there who are starving.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.290
We've gone there many times to help out.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:07.870
We in Chuohku are giving that camp
an enormous amount of assistance.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:12.950
I wonder what would happen to those children
if we terminated that assistance.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:15.370
--Is that a threat?
--Why, you!

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:17.330
Stand down!

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:20.830
All you've got to do is
what you've been told to do.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:26.250
Saburo, is there a way out?

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:29.620
I'm searching for one!
But my connection's been cut.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.330
I don't have Internet access!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.660
Then use this.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:36.580
This is a satellite link that
not even Chuohku is aware of.

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:38.870
Wow, how'd you get
a hold of something like this?

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.700
The military has access to various things.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:46.160
That ramen shop owner couldn't possibly
know how to escape from Chuohku, could he?

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:49.410
Tom, are you planning
to become one of their lackeys?

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:52.200
Don't worry. I have no intention of doing that.

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.160
"Notification Center"
"You have a new message!"

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:59.580
Take a look at this.
It's from one of my hacker friends.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:01.290
What's this?

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:06.000
Why would a video game creator from Dubai
want to know how to escape from Chuohku?

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.410
Isn't the timing just a little too perfect?

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:14.540
I realized that myself just now.
One of those nine people is my hacker friend.

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:16.200
Most likely Saburo Yamada.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:19.580
That you two would know
each other--it sure is a small world.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.950
So, what's the plan?

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:23.500
It's obvious.

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.500
I got a reply! I don't believe it!
He says he knows!

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:33.080
I would like to meet this
ramen shop owner friend of yours.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.450
Next time I'll introduce him to you.

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:37.040
Everyone, that way!

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:41.700
Jeez, what a grand reception!

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:43.500
See, what'd I tell you?

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:49.000
Then shall we perform our show here
with just the three of us and no opening acts?

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.620
Aw, come on!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.700
There's still this many of them?!

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:11.410
This is what it meaneth
to have the whole world against thee.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.200
Out of my way!

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.870
Fling Posse!

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:18.660
Here comes Beauty with the face of the Beast...

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:21.790
I lack the vigor henceforth
to oppose the headliner.

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:24.040
I'm all tapped out.

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:27.500
Thus ends the tale of our
humble bard and his companions.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:36.750
But as long as it's gotta end,
let's take to the stage in style one last time!

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:45.250
We can escape from here!

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:48.450
Are you all right, Saburo?

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.080
Here, take my hand.

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:52.910
Brother Ichi... Jiro...

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:56.500
Woah, there. When you fall, I'll be with you.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.700
Hifumi...

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:06.910
I forgot she had a canceller.

00:22:06.910 --> 00:22:09.950
A-ME-MURAAAA!

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:15.330
You made quite a fool out of me.

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:19.040
For your actions,
you deserve to die a thousand deaths.

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:20.910
Eh-hehe...
